Use MAX_STATIC_DATA of 500000.
When play begins, seed the random-number generator with 1234.

container is a kind of thing.
door is a kind of thing.
object-like is a kind of thing.
supporter is a kind of thing.
food is a kind of object-like.
key is a kind of object-like.
containers are openable, lockable and fixed in place. containers are usually closed.
door is openable and lockable.
object-like is portable.
supporters are fixed in place.
food is edible.
A room has a text called internal name.


The r_0 and the r_1 and the r_9 and the r_13 and the r_11 and the r_15 and the r_14 and the r_16 and the r_17 and the r_18 and the r_2 and the r_3 and the r_7 and the r_4 and the r_5 and the r_6 and the r_8 and the r_10 and the r_12 and the r_19 are rooms.

Understand "cubicle" as r_0.
The internal name of r_0 is "cubicle".
The printed name of r_0 is "-= Cubicle =-".
The cubicle part 0 is some text that varies. The cubicle part 0 is "You've entered a standard room. Your mind races to think of what kind of room would be standard. And then it hits you. Of course. You're in the cubicle. Let's see what's in here.

 You make out a bureau. You shudder, but continue examining the room.[if c_0 is open and there is something in the c_0] The bureau contains [a list of things in the c_0].[end if]".
The cubicle part 1 is some text that varies. The cubicle part 1 is "[if c_0 is open and the c_0 contains nothing] The bureau is empty, what a horrible day![end if]".
The cubicle part 2 is some text that varies. The cubicle part 2 is " You lean against the wall, inadvertently pressing a secret button. The wall opens up to reveal a stand. The stand is normal.[if there is something on the s_0] On the stand you can make out [a list of things on the s_0].[end if]".
The cubicle part 3 is some text that varies. The cubicle part 3 is "[if there is nothing on the s_0] Looks like someone's already been here and taken everything off it, though.[end if]".
The cubicle part 4 is some text that varies. The cubicle part 4 is "

You need an unguarded exit? You should try going east. You need an unguarded exit? You should try going north. There is an unguarded exit to the south. You need an unblocked exit? You should try going west.".
The description of r_0 is "[cubicle part 0][cubicle part 1][cubicle part 2][cubicle part 3][cubicle part 4]".

